  "reason": "RNA-only models are much stronger than image-only models, with scvi_n200 + multiprofile + transformer/avgpool giving the best validation accuracy and F1 (~0.65), while image-only models are weak (~0.21-0.23). The key remaining uncertainty is whether image features can complement the strong RNA representation in a multimodal model. config_038 keeps the strongest RNA setting (scvi_n200, multiprofile, transformer) and adds the better single-image encoder (ViT-L) with simple concat fusion, directly testing whether multimodal fusion improves over the best RNA-only baseline. This is the most informative next experiment before exploring weighted fusion or other image encoders."
